# TASK: Redesign "TeenaReader" (Android PDF reader) — Premium, Simple, Fast, Single-Source Theme

You are working on an existing Android PDF reader app (Kotlin + Jetpack Compose + Material 3).
Rename the app display name to **TeenaReader**.
DO NOT change business logic (PDF rendering, database, file scanning). Only redesign UI/theme and wire existing data into the new components.

## 0. WORKING RULES (READ FIRST, FOLLOW STRICTLY)

1. Work in the numbered STEPS below, in order. After each step, make sure the project compiles before moving on.
2. If an import is missing, add it. Do not invent new libraries except the ones listed in Step 1.
3. **ZERO hardcoding outside `ui/theme/`**: no `Color(0x..)`, no raw `dp`/`sp` for design values, no `FontFamily`, no `RoundedCornerShape(12.dp)`, no `tween(300)` in screens or components. Use only `MaterialTheme.*` and `TeenaTheme.*` tokens.
4. All user-visible text must be in `res/values/strings.xml` (use plurals for counts: "1 PDF", "2 PDFs").
5. **No Monospace font anywhere.**
6. The top bar has **NO icons** except: the search icon inside the search field, the clear (X) icon inside the search field, and the three-dots menu button.
7. Same top bar on every tab (Recent / Library / Folders). It must never change layout between tabs.
8. Titles: max 2 lines + ellipsis. Meta text: exactly 1 line. Never put more than 2 meta items in one line.
9. All `LazyColumn`/`LazyVerticalGrid` items must have `key` and `contentType`. All models passed to composables must be `@Immutable`.
10. Keep the existing ViewModels/repositories. If the existing model differs from `PdfItem` below, write a small mapper — do not rewrite the data layer.
11. At the end, run the Definition of Done checklist (Step 12) and report results.

